  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "            Spanish distinguishes between two verbs that translate as 'to be': 'ser' and 'estar'. \n' Ser' describes inherent or permanent characteristics, identity, origin and time (e.g., 'La casa es grande' – 'The house is large'). \n'Estar' is used for temporary conditions, location or ongoing actions (e.g., 'Estamos en la oficina' – 'We are in the office'). \nConfusing the two is a common mistake; understanding the difference helps you choose the appropriate verb in context.\n"
    }
